#### *Markdown Extraction Test*

This document checks whether a PDF extractor can recover ordinary Markdown structure without relying on complex
Carve features.
Text can be *bold*, /italic/, or /*bold and italic*/ . It can also contain a visible link.
note
The extended formatting line contains underlined text, highlighted text, superscript , and subscriptindex.

##### *Paragraphs*

This is the first paragraph. It wraps across more than one visual line in the PDF, but it should remain one paragraph in
the extracted Markdown.
This is a separate paragraph. The vertical space above it should prevent both paragraphs from being merged.

##### *Lists*

First unordered item
Second unordered item
Third unordered item

1. First ordered item
2. Second ordered item
3. Third ordered item

##### *Blockquote*

/Good extraction preserves the quotation as a blockquote instead of flattening it into an ordinary paragraph./

##### *Code*

function greet(string $name): string {
    return "Hello, {$name}!";
}

##### *Simple table*

*Region Revenue Growth*
North 1,240 13.7%
South 980 4.1%
Total 2,220 9.5%

##### *Literal punctuation*

The next lines are literal text, not Markdown constructs:

# not a heading

- not a list item
/not emphasis/, /not emphasis/, [not a link], 2 | 3, C:\docs\file, and a \`backtick.

